# Public changelog

`src/server/site/changelog.js` is the single source of truth for the changelog at
`/changelog`. It renders on both the Vercel build and the Express route.

## When to update it

Add an entry for anything a customer would notice: new panel features, Discord bot
capabilities, pricing or plan changes, marketing pages, and user-facing bug fixes.

Skip it for refactors, dependency bumps, internal tooling, and comment or test-only
changes.

## How to update it

Add to the **top** of `entries`. Reuse today's entry if one already exists for the
same date and it hasn't shipped yet; otherwise start a new one.

```js
{
  date: "2026-08-04",              // ISO, renders as "August 4, 2026"
  title: "Scheduled broadcasts",   // short, sentence case, no version numbers
  changes: [
    { type: "added", text: "Queue broadcasts to send on a repeating timer." },
    { type: "fixed", text: "Ban list paging skipped the last page." },
  ],
}
```

- `type` is only `added`, `changed`, or `fixed`.
- Write `text` for a server owner, not a developer: describe the capability, not the
  implementation. Say "Staff can now be limited to kick-only" rather than "refactored
  the permission resolver".
- One sentence per change, ending in a period. Inline HTML like `<code>` is allowed.

Do this in the same change as the feature, before committing.
